  "decline_reason": "",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "For the split, the Manual requires a divisional application identifying both the goods or services being divided out and those to remain in the parent.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part12/3#1",
          "quote": "the divisional application must specify the goods or services to which it relates; and the divisional application must be for some only of the goods or services of the parent application; and the divisional application must specify the goods or services that are to remain in the parent application."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Manual also requires the same trade mark and applicant, with the parent being a single application.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part12/3#1",
          "quote": "the trade marks must be the same; and the trade mark applicants must be the same; and the parent must be a single application;"
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "File the divisional while the parent is still pending and before deleting the goods or services being divided out from the parent.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part12/2#1",
          "quote": "The parent application must be pending at the time the divisional application is filed and the goods/services of the divisional application must still be present in the parent application at the time of filing."
        },
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part12/2#1",
          "quote": "Premature deletion or amendment of the goods/services of the parent may invalidate a subsequent divisional application."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "For this purpose, the Manual's checklist says that pending includes applications with “accepted” or “opposed” status.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part12/x-annex-a1-divisional-checklist-for-divisional-applications-filed-on-or-after-27-march-2007#1",
          "quote": "Pending includes status “accepted” and status “opposed”."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under the Manual's checklist, where there is no duplication or encompassment between the divisional goods or services and those specified to remain in the parent, and the divisional is valid and complete, the examiner must process the parent's exclusion amendment as soon as practicable.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part12/x-annex-a1-divisional-checklist-for-divisional-applications-filed-on-or-after-27-march-2007#1",
          "quote": "6. Are any of the goods/services of the divisional duplicated in or encompassed by the goods/services specified to remain in the parent?"
        },
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part12/x-annex-a1-divisional-checklist-for-divisional-applications-filed-on-or-after-27-march-2007#1",
          "quote": "If the answer to question 6 is no, and the divisional application is valid and complete, the examiner must (as soon as practicable) process the amendment to the specification of the parent application to exclude the claimed goods and/or services of the divisional application."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "For a late application for an award of costs or a late bill of costs, the Manual says consideration is conditional on obtaining an extension of time under section 224.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part55/3/3/4",
          "quote": "A late application for an award of costs, or a bill of costs that has been filed outside the time limit under reg 21.12, can only be considered if the person concerned is granted an extension of time under s 224."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lodge that extension application in an approved form, together with the appropriate fee and a supporting declaration.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part55/3/3/4",
          "quote": "Such an application for extension must be in an approved form and must be filed together with the appropriate fee and a supporting declaration (reg 21.25)."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "If the extension sought is for more than three months, the Manual says the extension application must be published for opposition.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part55/3/3/4",
          "quote": "If the extension of time sought is for a period greater than 3 months, the application must be published for the purposes of opposition (subsections 224(5) and (6))."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The supplied passages do not state the original costs filing deadline, a deadline for lodging the extension request, the fee amount, or whether the late costs document must accompany that request, so I cannot specify those details from this material.",
      "quotes": [],
      "authority": "none"
    },
    {
      "text": "These procedural requirements are reported here as Manual practice: the supplied legislation does not include sections 45, 46 or 224 or regulations 21.12 and 21.25, and the supplied material may not provide a complete filing checklist.",
      "quotes": [],
      "authority": "none"
    }
  ],
